  "problem": "Consider the following set of functions:\n\n$$\n{f}_{1}(t)=\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t,\\,{f}_{2}(t)=\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(3t),\\,{f}_{3}(t)=\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(5t)\n$$\n\nGiven that the inner product in the vector space $C[0,\\pi /2]$ of continuous functions over $[0,\\pi /2]$ is defined as \n\n$$\n\u27e8f(t),g(t)\u27e9={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}f(t)g(t)\\,\\text{d}t,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${f}_{1}(t)\u22a5{f}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product\n- ${f}_{1}(t)\u22a5{f}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product\n- $S={{f}_{1}(t),{f}_{2}(t),{f}_{3}(t)}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product\n\n*Hint: $\u27e8{f}_{2},{f}_{3}\u27e9=0.$*",
